  "content": {
    "id": "p19-q16-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "16",
    "prompt": "A rectangle has perimeter $20\\text{ cm}$. Both the length and width are whole numbers.\nList all possible rectangles and their areas. Which has the largest area?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Side lengths (cm) → area (cm²): $(9,1)\\to9$; $(8,2)\\to16$; $(7,3)\\to21$; $(6,4)\\to24$; $(5,5)\\to25$. The $5\\text{ cm}\\times5\\text{ cm}$ square has the largest area, $25\\text{ cm}^2$.",
      "worked": "The perimeter gives\n$$\\begin{align*}P&=2(l+w)\\\\20&=2(l+w)\\\\l+w&=10.\\end{align*}$$\nList the positive whole-number pairs once each and use $A=lw$:\n$$\\begin{align*}A_{9,1}&=9\\times1=9\\text{ cm}^2\\\\A_{8,2}&=8\\times2=16\\text{ cm}^2\\\\A_{7,3}&=7\\times3=21\\text{ cm}^2\\\\A_{6,4}&=6\\times4=24\\text{ cm}^2\\\\A_{5,5}&=5\\times5=25\\text{ cm}^2.\\end{align*}$$\nThe $5\\text{ cm}\\times5\\text{ cm}$ square has the largest area, $25\\text{ cm}^2$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 60
  },
